// Item definitions (ARCHITECTURE.md §7). `block` is the numeric block-state
// id an item places, until the data-driven block registry replaces the
// hardcoded ids. Namespaced string ids are the stable identity (§7.6).
// `category` groups items into creative-inventory tabs (data-driven).
[
    (id: "oc:stone",  name: "Stone",       block: Some(1),  category: "building"),
    (id: "oc:dirt",   name: "Dirt",        block: Some(2),  category: "natural"),
    (id: "oc:grass",  name: "Grass Block", block: Some(3),  category: "natural"),
    (id: "oc:sand",   name: "Sand",        block: Some(4),  category: "building"),
